            <INNER_RULE APP_VERSION="8.5.5-6" CACHE_TTL="864000" CACHE_TTL_SYNCED="true" CLASSIFICATION="REG_STATUS" DESCRIPTION="Computer Object searches AD computer objects where the 'objectCategory' property is 'computer'.&#10;&#10;Each unique value of the Forescout 'hostname' or 'hostnames_list' property is used to search the AD 'dNSHostName' property, using 'dNSHostName={hostname}' or 'dNSHostName={hostnames_list}'. A short name without a DNS suffix instead searches the AD 'sAMAccountName' property with a trailing '$'.&#10;&#10;If the initial name search finds no matching object, the app splits each fully qualified DNS name into its first label and remaining DNS suffix. The first label becomes a computer account name, such as 'sAMAccountName=computer01$'.&#10;&#10;This fallback is permitted when the DNS suffix equals the connection's configured AD domain or is a child DNS suffix of that domain.&#10;&#10;For a connection configured for 'example.com':&#10;- 'computer01.example.com' has an exact domain match. The fallback searches for 'sAMAccountName=computer01$' in 'example.com'.&#10;- 'computer01.department.example.com' has a child DNS suffix, 'department.example.com'. Because it ends in '.example.com', the fallback searches for 'sAMAccountName=computer01$' in the configured parent domain, 'example.com'. It does not search 'department.example.com' or assume that a separate AD domain exists there.&#10;- 'computer01.other.com' has an unrelated DNS suffix. If the initial full-name search finds nothing, no account-name fallback is attempted.&#10;&#10;All searches remain within the current connection's AD domain and search base. Account names are matched exactly; only the DNS suffix allows the parent-domain relationship. Confidence remains Low because DNS information can be stale or identify an alias." ID="-4798033088837576496" NAME="[Low Confidence] Object Found" NOT_COND_UPDATE="true" RECHECK_MAIN_RULE_DEF="true">
